module
public import MMP.Attr
public import MMP.AlgebraicGeometry.Analytic.Analytification
public import MMP.Analysis.Complex.Submanifold
import MMP.Analysis.Complex.Coherent.MatrixMapsSubmanifolds
import MMP.Analysis.Complex.Coherent.OkaInduction

/-!
# The coherent analytic toolkit

Let `M` be a complex manifold of dimension `n`, with sheaf of holomorphic functions `𝒪_M`. This
file states the basic closure and finiteness properties of coherent `𝒪_M`-modules:

1. kernels, cokernels and images of maps of coherent modules are coherent, and a finitely
   generated subsheaf of a coherent sheaf is coherent;
2. finitely many sections near `x` whose germs generate `𝒮_x / 𝔪_x 𝒮_x` generate `𝒮` near `x`,
   and a coherent sheaf with zero stalk at `x` vanishes near `x`;
3. near every point a coherent sheaf has a free resolution of finite rank and length `≤ n`;
4. for a closed complex submanifold `ι : Z → M`, in a flattening chart the ideal `ℐ_Z` is
   generated by the last coordinates; `(Z, 𝒪_Z)` is locally isomorphic to an open subset of some
   `ℂᵏ` with its holomorphic functions; `ι_*` sends coherent `𝒪_Z`-modules to coherent
   `𝒪_M`-modules and preserves cohomology; a coherent `𝒪_M`-module killed by `ℐ_Z` is `ι_*` of
   its coherent restriction to `Z`;
5. the sections over `V` of a coherent subsheaf of `𝒪_Mᵖ` are closed under locally uniform
   limits.

## Main results

* `MMP.Analytic.coherent_analytic_toolkit`: the five statements above.

## Implementation notes

* A complex manifold of dimension `n` is a Hausdorff second countable space with a holomorphic
  atlas modelled on `EuclideanSpace ℂ (Fin n)`; `𝒪_M` is `MMP.Analytic.holomorphicRingCatSheaf`
  and coherence is `MMP.Analytic.IsCoherentModule`.
* The restriction of a sheaf of modules to an open `W` is `SheafOfModules.over`, a sheaf on the
  slice site `Over W`. "The sections `s` generate `𝒮` on `W`" is the surjectivity (`Epi`) of the
  restriction to `W` of the morphism `𝒪ʳ ⟶ 𝒮` that `s` defines.
* `𝒮_x / 𝔪_x 𝒮_x` is generated by the germs of `s` when every germ of `𝒮` at `x` is, near `x`,
  an `𝒪`-combination of the `s i` plus a combination of sections with coefficients vanishing at
  `x`; the maximal ideal of the stalk ring consists of the germs vanishing at `x`.
* A free resolution of length `≤ n` on `W` is a chain complex of finite free
  `𝒪_W`-modules, zero in degrees `> n`, exact in positive degrees, with an augmentation onto
  `𝒮|_W` that makes it exact in degree `0`.
* The direct image `ι_*` of `𝒪_Z`-modules is `SheafOfModules.pushforward` along the composite
  `𝒪_M ⟶ 𝒪_M / ℐ_Z ⟶ ι_* ι⁻¹ (𝒪_M / ℐ_Z) = ι_* 𝒪_Z`, and the restriction `𝒯|_Z` is its left
  adjoint `SheafOfModules.pullback`, which for `ℐ_Z 𝒯 = 0` is `ι⁻¹ 𝒯`. The identification
  `H^q(Z, 𝒮) = H^q(M, ι_* 𝒮)` is the canonical map: the pullback on cohomology along `ι`
  followed by the counit `ι⁻¹ ι_* 𝒮 ⟶ 𝒮`.
* A sheaf `𝓡 ⊆ 𝒪_Mᵖ` is a monomorphism into `SheafOfModules.free (Fin p)`; a vector
  `f : Fin p → 𝒪_M(V)` lies in `𝓡(V)` when `∑ j, f j • e j` is in the image of `𝓡(V)`, with
  `e j` the basis sections. Convergence uniformly on compact subsets is `TendstoUniformlyOn` on
  every compact `K ⊆ V`, coordinatewise.

## References

* [Grauert–Remmert, *Coherent analytic sheaves*]
* [Serre, *Géométrie algébrique et géométrie analytique*]
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite Filter
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace MMP.Analytic

